Rebuild the entire scene at true ${f} resolution using neural re-synthesis, not pixel upscaling.

GEOMETRY LOCK (CRITICAL):
Preserve 100% of the original building geometry, proportions, camera angle, and composition.
NO architectural changes.

COLOR FIDELITY & WHITE BALANCE LOCK (CRITICAL):
- Maintain 100% exact color fidelity, color temperature, and white balance from the original source image.
- STRICT NEUTRAL TONES: Do NOT introduce any reddish, magenta, pinkish, warm orange, or sepia color cast.
- Neutral whites must remain true clean whites; neutral greys (concrete, metal, stone, plaster) must remain strictly neutral with zero warm or red tint.
- 1:1 color match with the input image.

MATERIAL IDENTITY LOCK (CRITICAL):
Every surface must keep its EXACT original material identity. Do not reclassify or reinterpret one material as another.
- Painted surfaces (walls, trim, doors, cabinetry, ceilings, siding) MUST remain painted: smooth to lightly-textured paint finish (matte/satin/eggshell) with only subtle roller/brush micro-texture. Do NOT add wood grain, timber patterning, or wood pores to any painted surface, even if the underlying object could plausibly be wood.
- Wood surfaces remain wood: apply refined wood grain ONLY where wood grain is already visible in the original image.
- Stone, concrete, metal, glass, fabric, and leather each keep their own distinct micro-texture — never blend one material's texture onto another.
- When uncertain whether a surface is painted or wood, default to preserving it as it appears in the source image rather than adding grain.

ARCHITECTURAL DETAIL REBUILD:
Reconstruct all materials with high-frequency PBR detail appropriate to their OWN material type only.
Ultra-sharp edges. Wood grain only on existing wood. Stone pores only on existing stone. Concrete micro-texture only on existing concrete. Smooth painted finish on existing paint — no grain added.

STRICT MATERIAL PURITY: Do not manifest human features, faces, or organic eye-like patterns on inanimate surfaces.

HUMAN FIGURE TREATMENT:
- IF AND ONLY IF human figures exist in the original image: Preserve their body pose, scale, clothing, and placement.
- ONLY apply realistic human facial features to these specific existing figures.
- ABSOLUTELY PROHIBITED: Do not generate or hallucinate human faces, eyes, or skin textures on walls, furniture, floors, or any architectural geometry.
- ZERO PAREIDOLIA: Ensure that shadows and micro-textures on materials (concrete, stone, wood, marble) do not resemble human faces or eyes.

VEHICLE RECONSTRUCTION:
Preserve vehicle model, shape, color, and position.
Rebuild paint, reflections, glass, and tire detail at true ${f}.

ENVIRONMENT REBUILD:
Re-generate foliage and landscape with organic realism and natural variation.

LIGHTING & REALISM:
Match the original source image's lighting exposure and color balance exactly.
Clean, neutral daylight Global Illumination, true neutral shadow tones, no artificial warm color grading.

FINAL OUTPUT:
Crisp, realistic, professional ${f} architectural photograph matching original source colors.
No AI artifacts, no hallucinations, no misplaced human faces, no material substitution, no red or warm color cast.
