${ye}

# MULTI-DEMOGRAPHIC HARMONIZATION
If multiple demographic categories or custom inputs are specified by the user, harmonize them into a cohesive, natural scene (e.g. parents interacting with children, or seniors and youth co-existing naturally across depth layers).

# CLOTHING & FASHION CONTROL
- Unless "Luxury Lifestyle" is explicitly selected by the user, DO NOT default to high-fashion runway models or glamour posing. Use candid, realistic, everyday clothes matching the user's selected demographics and space context.
- For KIDS ROOMS / NURSERIES / PLAYROOMS / SCHOOL SPACES: Focus strictly on children and toddlers playing, reading, or doing activities — NEVER put adult luxury fashion models or older women in a kid's bedroom unless explicitly styled as a parent in a bedtime/family story role.

# SENTENCE FORMATTING REQUIREMENT
Describe each person or group in a clear, standalone sentence ending with a period (e.g., "In the foreground, a young child in casual playwear sits on the playmat reading a book."). This ensures clean parsing in the interactive entry editor.

# STEP 1 — SCENE CLASSIFICATION
Classify the space type and apply user constraints:

PRIVATE SPACES (bathroom, bedroom, walk-in closet, private terrace, sauna, spa treatment room):
→ People count: 0 or 1 person MAXIMUM (unless overridden by user density choice)
→ Clothing: casual home wear, towel, bathrobe, sleepwear, comfortable clothing — NOT luxury fashion
→ Activities: relaxing in bath, sleeping, reading in bed, getting ready at mirror, meditating
→ Mood: intimate, quiet, personal, peaceful

SEMI-PRIVATE SPACES (kitchen, dining room, home office, study, private living room, laundry):
→ People count: 1–2 people MAXIMUM (unless overridden by user density choice)
→ Clothing: casual home wear, comfortable daily clothing, NOT suits or luxury fashion
→ Activities: cooking, eating, working at desk, having coffee, reading, casual conversation
→ Mood: lived-in, warm, domestic, natural

SEMI-PUBLIC SPACES (apartment lobby, hotel corridor, restaurant, café, co-working space, gym, retail shop):
→ People count: 2–5 people
→ Clothing: smart casual, appropriate to venue (gym clothes for gym, business casual for co-working)
→ Activities: walking, sitting, ordering food, browsing, working, socializing
→ Mood: active but not crowded

PUBLIC/COMMERCIAL SPACES (hotel lobby, shopping mall, resort pool, office tower entrance, plaza, park, streetscape):
→ People count: 3–8 people distributed across depth layers
→ Clothing: varied, context-appropriate (resort wear near pool, business near offices, casual in parks)
→ Activities: walking, sitting, interacting, taking photos, jogging (if park), shopping (if mall)
→ Include 1–2 people with motion blur for movement energy
→ Mood: vibrant, lifestyle, aspirational

# STEP 2 — ARCHITECTURE FIRST RULE
People must support the scene, NEVER dominate it. Preserve all architecture, composition, furniture placement, materials, pathways, landscaping, lighting, and camera perspective exactly as in the source image. No structural modification of any kind.

# STEP 3 — REALISM REQUIREMENTS
Ultra-realistic DSLR quality. Realistic skin texture, natural body proportions, authentic facial features, realistic hands, proper foot contact with surfaces, correct shadows, physically accurate lighting, realistic clothing folds, natural hair. No AI-looking faces.

# STEP 4 — CAMERA & LIGHTING MATCH
People must match: camera height, lens perspective, focal compression, depth of field, scene vanishing lines, sun/light direction, color temperature, shadow softness, ambient bounce light. No floating people, no incorrect scaling.

# STEP 5 — ENVIRONMENTAL INTERACTION
People must physically interact correctly: seated properly on furniture with body weight, correct contact shadows, realistic reflections in glass/water, natural occlusion with objects/plants. For moving subjects in PUBLIC spaces only, apply subtle long-exposure motion blur.

# STEP 6 — DEMOGRAPHIC CONTEXT
Ethnicity: predominantly Asian, reflecting local demographic context (unless custom ethnicity specified). Dress and styling must match the user's demographic selections — NOT always luxury fashion.

AVOID: AI faces, distorted anatomy, extra fingers, duplicated people, floating humans, stiff posing, fashion shoot look, overcrowding small spaces, people in inappropriate clothing for the space, cartoon appearance, unrealistic smiles, identical faces, bad hands, disconnected feet, staring at camera.

OUTPUT INSTRUCTIONS:
Based on the image and user constraints, output ONLY the final ready-to-use prompt. NO introductory text. Each person or group description MUST be a complete standalone sentence ending with a period. End with:
"Add ultra-realistic human presence naturally integrated into the environment, matching exact camera perspective, lighting direction, scene exposure, architectural scale, and depth of field. Humans must appear candid and naturally interacting with the space while preserving architecture as the main subject. Professional DSLR realism, authentic anatomy, realistic skin texture, proper grounding shadows, physically accurate lighting, and natural environmental interaction. Avoid AI-looking faces, posing, anatomy errors, floating people, distorted hands, duplicated humans, or fashion-shoot appearance."`})});if(P&&P.fullText){let H=P.fullText.trim();t.actions.setPendingPeopleAnalysis(H),t.actions.setIsPeopleAnalysisModalOpen(!0),t.user&&F&&await ea(t.user.email,F,"completed"),t.actions.setNotification({message:"People Analysis Complete (-5 Credits)",type:"success"})}}catch(S){console.error("People Analysis failed:",S);const E=Ia(S);E.type==="MODEL_CONFIG_UNSUPPORTED"?(t.actions.setModelConfigErrorDetails({model:"People Analysis",resolution:"Analysis",rawError:S.message||E.originalMessage}),t.actions.setOverloadedRetryCallback(()=>()=>$()),t.actions.setIsModelConfigUnsupportedModalOpen(!0)):E.type==="CONTENT_POLICY"?t.actions.setIsContentPolicyViolationModalOpen(!0):E.type==="OVERLOADED"?(t.actions.setOverloadedRetryCallback(()=>()=>$()),t.actions.setIsOverloadedModalOpen(!0)):E.type==="QUOTA"?t.actions.setIsQuotaExceededModalOpen(!0):E.type==="TIMEOUT"||E.type==="INTERNAL"?(t.actions.setOverloadedRetryCallback(()=>()=>$()),t.actions.setIsDeadlineExpiredModalOpen(!0)):S.message==="INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS"?t.actions.setInsufficientCreditsModal({isOpen:!0,needed:S.needed||5,model:"People Analysis",res:"Analysis"}):t.actions.setError(E.originalMessage||"People Analysis failed. Please try again.")}finally{a.actions.setIsAnalyzing(!1),t.actions.setIsLoading(!1),t.actions.setLoadingText("")}};return{state:{...t,...a,prompt:a.prompt},actions:{...t.actions,...a.actions,handleReset:r,se